@meeting vesselHome
// SW4, the Veyli vessel: Monday Day 29, 15:00-15:20, the shuttle bay, the Tern's ramp. About 15 (Works and friends).
// Taavek gives you a sketch (it goes to your shelf: the ring on Tuesday). The wave pose on Taavek's last line.
// Lindqvist, called in on his day off, flies them across.
title: Taavek goes home
from: Taavek
gist: You saw Taavek off at the Tern's ramp. They gave you a sketch, labelled in Veyli: "For you. The one who meets."
== lines
calder: Ramp's down. Part's packed. Say it now, if you're saying it.   [nod]
taavek: Three sketches. One for my ship. One for your bay, by the tools.   [gesture]
taavek > you: And one for you. The one who meets.   [gesture]
? choice
* I'll put it on my shelf.   flavour:share rel:taavek+1
  taavek: Good. A shelf is a good place. On my shelf, your ship.   [nod]
* Come back and see it.   flavour:cheer rel:taavek+1
  taavek: Yes. When we pass, I knock. Loudly.   [laugh]
* What does the writing say?   flavour:listen rel:taavek+1
  taavek: "For you. The one who meets." And your name. Badly. I practise.   [laugh]
lindqvist-isak: My day off, and I'd fly this one twice. Strapped in? She wants to go.   [gesture]
taavek: Go well. Go well, Wren.   [gesture]
calder: Good part. Back to it.   [nod]
